h", "medium", "low"], "title": "Qualitative Confidence", "type": "string"}, "uncertainty": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Uncertainty", "type": "array"}, "conditions_that_change_market_read": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Conditions That Change Market Read", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["schema", "role", "decision", "symbol", "decision_time_ms", "market_context", "setup", "decision_timeframe", "context_timeframes_used", "entry_mechanism", "trigger", "invalidation", "evidence_for", "evidence_against", "qualitative_confidence", "uncertainty", "conditions_that_change_market_read"], "title": "TradeIntentV2", "type": "object"}
Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790081999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790035199999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The strongest counterargument: the largest single directional move in the window is the opening 12-bar, ~36% bear leg to 1368.42, so the bull-trend label rests only on the last ~34 bars, and the 73 bars before that are balance, not trend.", "The 27 bars ahead of the final push are a two-sided range (2357.18-2680) with heavy overlap and mid-range closes; 2850 is a first-bar probe only 79.00 above 2771, and single-bar breakouts of multi-week range tops often fail and re-enter the range.", "Bar 1787270400000 (445.69 range, close 2515.30, ~255.70 upper tail) followed by a 27-bar stall is spike-high behavior consistent with a temporary exhaustion and a market capped by a range boundary rather than a functioning bull channel.", "The 208.30-point final bar after an extended advance could be a buy climax; a large bull bar that is immediately retraced would mark exhaustion rather than breakout acceptance."], "evidence_for": ["A 388.17-point bull trend bar (1787097600000) closed at 2252.16, 89% of its range and above the 73-bar range top 1974.46, with immediate follow-through to 2771 two bars later.", "Successive higher swing highs across the window (1974.46, 2293.80, 2771, 2850) and higher swing lows (1368.42, 1512.91, 2357.18/2358.62).", "The 27-bar pause held entirely above the breakout bar's open 1916.51 and the old range top 1974.46; no close returned inside the 73-bar range.", "The final bar closes 2775.61 above the prior spike high 2771 and in the upper 64% of its range, with four consecutive rising closes."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["The window opens at 2109.85 (close of 1779667200000) after a 2139.34 high, then declines 13 bars to 1368.42 (low of 1780704000000), about 36% below 2139.34.", "Bar 1780704000000 has a 230.85 range with a 200.13 lower tail and closes at 1568.55 (top ~13% of its range); bar 1780790400000 (open 1568.55, high 1690.78, low 1563.52, close 1687.83) is a bull reversal bar closing at its high.", "From 1780790400000 to 1787011200000 (73 bars) price overlaps repeatedly between 1512.91 (low of 1782432000000) and 1974.46 (high of 1785110400000); closes cluster 1550-1950 with many overlapping bodies and mixed closes (two-sided range).", "Bar 1787097600000 breaks out: open 1916.51, high 2293.80, low 1905.63, close 2252.16, a 388.17-point bull trend bar closing in the top ~11% of its range and above the 1974.46 range top.", "Bar 1787270400000 spikes to 2771 with a 445.69 range, closing 2515.30 and leaving a ~255.70 upper tail.", "Bars 1787184000000 through 1789603200000 (27 bars) stay between 2357.18 (low of 1788307200000) and 2680 (high of 1789084800000); bodies overlap and closes sit mostly 2380-2530.", "The last four closes are 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61; the final bar (open 2642.90, high 2850, low 2641.70, close 2775.61) closes above the prior spike high 2771 in the upper 64% of its 208.30-point range."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bear leg of 13 bars from the window high 2139.34 into the 1368.42 low of 1780704000000; bar ranges expand into the low and that bar closes 1568.55 with a 200.13 lower tail, followed by a bull reversal bar at 1687.83.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779667200000, "upper_boundary": "2139.34"}, {"description": "73-bar two-sided range from 1780790400000 to 1787011200000; repeated overlap between 1512.91 and 1974.46 with a slight upward tilt after the 1512.91 low, many inside bars and closes in the middle of the range.", "end_time_ms": 1787183999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike escaping the 73-bar range: bar 1787097600000 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16 above the 1974.46 range top, with follow-through to the 2771 spike high of 1787270400000.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Post-spike pause of 27 bars between the 2357.18 low of 1788307200000 and the 2680 high of 1789084800000; most highs sit 2520-2560 with probes to 2680 and most lows 2357-2440, heavy body overlap and mid-range closes.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787184000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Final bull leg from the 2358.62 low of bar 1789430400000: 1789689600000 and 1789776000000 close 2612.02 and 2632.98, and 1789948800000 closes 2775.61 above the 2771 spike high. The breakout proper is bars 1789689600000-1789948800000.", "end_time_ms": 1790035199999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation: several consecutive closes holding above 2700 (high of 1789776000000) and above 2771, with higher lows above 2641.70, would confirm acceptance above the spike high and strengthen the bull-trend/breakout-spike read.", "Failed breakout: a close back below 2641.70 (low of the final bar), followed by a close below 2568.16 (low of 1789862400000), would signal the breakout failed and shift the read back toward the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Range reassertion: a close back below 2357.18 with follow-through would turn the post-spike structure into a top and recast the 1787097600000 advance as a bull trap.", "Trend weakening: deeper pullbacks that overlap prior swing lows together with more bear bars closing near their lows would move the phase from breakout-spike toward channel or range.", "Climax risk: a further outsized bull bar immediately followed by a bear bar closing near its low would argue for a buy climax rather than a sustained second leg."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790078399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["96 of the 120 bars sit inside a 2358.62-2609.02 trading range with complete givebacks of prior spikes (bar 1788436800000 close 2506.79 later traded to 2450.96; bar 1789128000000 high 2680.00 later traded to 2479.76), so a whole-window trading-range read remains defensible.", "The 2850.00 breakout bar closed 2723.15, 126.85 below its high and in the lower third of its range, and the next five bars made lower highs with no close above 2775.61 - the breakout above 2800 has no follow-through yet.", "The last six bars overlap in a 2716.01-2804.59 box with two bear closes (2738.87, 2724.95), so short-term Always-In has flipped down inside the pullback and is not currently long with high relevance.", "Both earlier bull spikes in this window fully failed, so an unresolved spike into the window high has direct precedent for reversing.", "The advance from 2568.16 to 2850.00 is only ~24 bars at the very right edge of a 120-bar window whose body is a range; the trend label rests on recent bars, not on the window majority."], "evidence_for": ["Since the 2358.62 low (bar 1789488000000) the window prints a ~40-bar run of higher swing lows (2435.71, 2486.12, 2568.16, 2646.02, 2716.01) and higher swing highs (2438.47, 2481.66, 2585.50, 2643.52, 2700.00, 2850.00), the textbook definition of a bull leg.", "The 2609.02 range high was broken by two large bull bars (closes 2578.60 and 2636.28) and the following 15-bar flag held above 2568.16 rather than falling back into the 96-bar range - acceptance rather than a one-bar poke.", "The active pullback retraces only ~48% of the 2568.16-2850.00 leg and holds above the 2700.00 breakout level, so bears have not reclaimed the prior structure.", "Advance bars close near their highs (bar 1789704000000 close 2578.60 vs high 2585.50; bar 1789747200000 close 2636.28 vs high 2643.52; bar 1789977600000 reaches 2850.00), and the sequence of spikes separated by flags is a trending channel, not a neutral two-sided range at the right edge.", "The last bar is a bull bar closing at 2740.20 in the upper half of its range, and no bar in the pullback closed below 2716.01."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["All 120 closed H4 bars are present. Window high 2850.00 at bar 1789977600000, window low 2358.62 at bar 1789488000000, and the last close 2740.20 sits in the upper ~22% of that 491.38-point window range.", "Bars 1788350400000-1789718400000 (96 bars) overlap repeatedly inside 2358.62-2609.02 with many small dojis (e.g., bar 1788595200000 high 2458.92 low 2451.81, range 7.11) and no sustained directional sequence.", "Two bull spikes out of that range were given back: bar 1788436800000 closed 2506.79 after a 2404.35-2509.15 range and price later closed 2450.96 (bar 1788523200000); bar 1789128000000 closed 2555.52 with a 2680.00 high and price closed 2479.76 eleven bars later (bar 1789286400000).", "From the 2358.62 low, pullback lows keep rising: 2435.71 (1789646400000), 2486.12 (1789718400000), 2568.16 (1789891200000), 2646.02 (1789963200000), 2716.01 (1790049600000), while swing highs step up 2438.47 (1789603200000), 2481.66 (1789646400000), 2585.50 (1789732800000), 2643.52 (1789747200000), 2700.00 (1789804800000), 2850.00 (1789977600000).", "Breakout bars: bar 1789732800000 (open 2507.15, close 2578.60) and bar 1789747200000 (open 2579.97, close 2636.28 near its 2643.52 high) close above the 2609.02 prior range high, then 15 bars (1789761600000-1789963200000) overlap in a 2568.16-2700.00 box with contracting ranges (smallest 20.37 at bar 1789848000000).", "Bar 1789977600000 (open 2658.81, high 2850.00, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) is a 191.94-point bull spike that closes 126.85 below its high, in the lower third of its range; no later bar closes above 2775.61.", "The five bars after that high make lower highs (2795.00, 2804.59, 2776.18, 2741.20, 2752.61) and hold a low of 2716.01, which is above the 2700.00 breakout level; the final bar (open 2724.95, high 2752.61, low 2722.76, close 2740.20) is a small bull bar closing in the upper half of its range after two bear closes (2738.87, 2724.95).", "The 2850.00-2716.01 pullback gives back 133.99 of the 281.84-point 2568.16-2850.00 leg (~48%) without reclaiming the 2700.00 breakout level."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Dominant 96-bar trading range: bars 1788350400000-1789718400000 repeatedly overlap between the 2358.62 low and the 2609.02 high, and every spike leg out of it is largely given back within a few bars.", "end_time_ms": 1789718400000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1788350400000, "upper_boundary": "2609.02"}, {"description": "Bull breakout of the range: bar 1789732800000 (open 2507.15, high 2585.50, close 2578.60) and bar 1789747200000 (open 2579.97, high 2643.52, close 2636.28) close above the 2609.02 range high - the only sustained acceptance above that level in the window.", "end_time_ms": 1789747200000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789732800000, "upper_boundary": null}, {"description": "Fifteen-bar bull flag after the breakout: bars 1789761600000-1789963200000 overlap in a 2568.16-2700.00 box with contracting ranges (smallest 20.37 at bar 1789848000000) and hold far above the 2609.02 breakout level.", "end_time_ms": 1789963200000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2568.16", "start_time_ms": 1789761600000, "upper_boundary": "2700.00"}, {"description": "Second bull spike: bar 1789977600000 (open 2658.81, high 2850.00, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) breaks the 2700.00 flag high but closes 126.85 off its high in the lower third of its 191.94 range, so the breakout bar was sold into immediately.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": null}, {"description": "Six-bar pullback/consolidation under the 2850.00 high: bars 1789992000000-1790064000000 overlap between 2716.01 and 2804.59 with lower highs (2795.00, 2804.59, 2776.18, 2741.20, 2752.61) while holding above the 2700.00 breakout level.", "end_time_ms": 1790064000000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2716.01", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Possible mtr-like topping shape: a climactic bull spike to 2850.00 (bar 1789977600000) with a 126.85 upper tail, then a lower high at 2804.59 (bar 1790020800000). It is only a named possibility, not a reversal, while 2700.00 holds and no bear bar closes below the 2716.01 pullback low.", "end_time_ms": 1790064000000, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": null}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation: a close above 2804.59 (bar 1790020800000 high) that then accepts above 2850.00 confirms the flag breakout and keeps the bull-trend/channel read with rising Always-In relevance.", "Reversal: consecutive closes below 2716.01 (bar 1790049600000 low) and then below 2700.00 put price back inside the 2568.16-2700.00 flag and shift the read toward trading-range or an mtr-like reversal of the 2358.62-2850.00 leg.", "Continued overlap strictly inside 2716.01-2804.59 with no boundary break degrades the read to a two-sided pullback/range with low Always-In relevance.", "A close below 2568.16 would break the last higher swing low and mark the 2358.62-2850.00 advance as a completed leg.", "A new spike bar that closes above 2850.00 without a lar